    "text": "Her is halwendlic lar and \u00f0earflic l\u00e6wedum mannum, \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6t l\u00e6den ne cunnon.\nMen \u00f0a leofestan, gehyra\u00f0, hw\u00e6t us halige bec beoda\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t we for godes lufan and for his ege ure lif\nAnd uton eallon m\u00e6gne us scyldan wi\u00f0 ofermodignesse, for\u00f0am \u00fee hy awurpon iu englas of heofonum,\nFor\u00f0i is \u00e6lcum men ofer\u00feearf, \u00fe\u00e6t he him georne wi\u00f0 \u00feone leahter gebeorge, \u00fee l\u00e6s \u00fee him beo\nAnd utan don, swa us mycel \u00feearf ys, forbugan geornlice \u00fea synleahtras, \u00fee us forbodene synd, \u00fe\u00e6t is\nWe halsia\u00f0 eow and beoda\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t ge god lufian and him eallunga gehyrsume beon, for\u00f0am us ys neod,\nUtan nu, leofan men, ge\u00feencan \u00feone nacodan lichoman, \u00fee we on \u00f0as woruld brohton, \u00fe\u00e6t we hine\nAnd uton ge\u00feencan, \u00fe\u00e6t us ys uncu\u00f0 seo tid and se d\u00e6g, \u00fee we sceolon \u00feas l\u00e6nan woruld forl\u00e6ton and\n\u00d0onne ne bi\u00f0 nan \u00feing, \u00fe\u00e6s \u00fee we \u00e6fre gefremedon godes o\u00f0\u00f0e yfeles, godes \u00e6lmihtiges eagum\nFor\u00f0am we bidda\u00f0 eow and beoda\u00f0 on godes naman and on his haligra, \u00fe\u00e6t ge beorgan eow wi\u00f0 \u00feone\nSelre us ic mycele and \u00f0earflicre, \u00fe\u00e6t we ure gyltas andetton anum men her on life, \u00feonne we sceolon\n\u00d0\u00e6r nan man ne m\u00e6g n\u00e6nig \u00f0ing forhelan ne bediglian, ac \u00f0\u00e6r sceal \u00e6ghwylc man onfon \u00feam rihtan\nUton ge\u00feencan, to hwam \u00fea gewurdan, \u00fee beforan us w\u00e6ron, and to hwam we gewur\u00f0an sceolon.\nAnd gyf hwylc man sy, \u00fe\u00e6t ne cunne his pater noster and his credan, beo he swy\u00f0e geornlice embe, \u00fe\u00e6t\nAnd f\u00e6sta\u00f0 eower lenctenf\u00e6sten rihtlice to nones \u00e6lc man, \u00fee beo ofer xii wintre, and \u00f0a feower\nAnd we cy\u00fea\u00f0 eow, \u00fe\u00e6t god \u00e6lmihtig cw\u00e6\u00f0 his agenum mu\u00f0e, \u00fe\u00e6t nan man ne mot abyrgean nanes\nNu, leofan menn, uton don, swa man us bit and l\u00e6r\u00f0, ge\u00feencan, hu feallendlic and hu l\u00e6nendlic and hu\nUton don, swa us mycel \u00feearf ys, ondr\u00e6don us \u00feone micclan dom and \u00f0a micclan wita, \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6r beo\u00f0\nEall eor\u00f0e bifa\u00f0, and ealle duna dreosa\u00f0 and hreosa\u00f0, and \u00f0a beorgas buga\u00f0 and mylta\u00f0, and se egeslica\n\u00d0onne ahreosa\u00f0 ealle steorran ny\u00f0er, and seo sunne forswyrc\u00f0 sona on morgen, and se mona n\u00e6f\u00f0 nane\nAnd \u00f0onne cuma\u00f0 hider adune of heofonum dea\u00f0 beacnigende tacn and brega\u00f0 \u00fea earman; \u00feonne\nSit \u00feonne se m\u00e6ra heofonlica dema on his heahsettle helme gewur\u00feod; and we beo\u00f0 him \u00feonne f\u00e6ringa\nNu, leofan men, uton habban us on mycelum gemynde, hu mycel se broga bi\u00f0 \u00e6tforan godes domsetle,\n\u00deonne bi\u00f0 gebann mycel \u00feyder aboden, eall Adames cynn eor\u00f0bugjendra, \u00fee on foldan wear\u00f0 \u00e6fre\n\u00de\u00e6r swutela\u00f0 \u00e6lc cild, hwa hit formyr\u00f0rode.\n\u00de\u00e6r beo\u00f0 \u00feonne ealra manna digle ge\u00feancas geopenode on \u00fe\u00e6re d\u00e6gtide.\nEall, \u00fe\u00e6t seo heorte hearmes ge\u00f0ohte o\u00f0\u00f0e seo tunge to teonan geclypode o\u00f0\u00f0e mannes hand man\nAnd eac \u00feonne bi\u00f0 gefylled eall uplic lyft \u00e6trenum lige, f\u00e6r\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t fyr ofer eall, ne by\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6r nan\n\u00deonne nele ne wrecenda lig and se deoflica bryne \u00e6nine forbugan, buton he \u00e6ror beo her afeormod\n\u00d0onne of fela \u00feeodum folc orm\u00e6tlice mycel hyra synnigan breost swy\u00f0e beata\u00f0 forhte mid fystum for\n\u00de\u00e6r beo\u00f0 \u00feonne \u00feearfan and \u00f0eodcyningas, earme and eadige ealle af\u00e6rede.\n\u00d0\u00e6r h\u00e6f\u00f0 ane lage se earma and se eadiga, for\u00f0on hi ealle habba\u00f0 ege \u00feone m\u00e6stan.\nNu we magon sylfe \u00feus to urum lichaman sprecan: hw\u00e6t dest \u00feu, la fl\u00e6sc, o\u00f0\u00f0e hw\u00e6t drihst \u00feu nu?\nHw\u00e6t miht \u00feu on \u00fea tid \u00feearfe wepan?\nWa \u00f0e nu, \u00f0u \u00fee \u00feeowast \u00f0issere worulde and her on galnysse leofast.\nHwi ne forhttast \u00feu \u00f0e fyrene egesan and \u00fee sylfum ondr\u00e6tst swi\u00f0lice witu, \u00fea drihten geo deoflum\nNe m\u00e6g nan eor\u00f0lic man eall areccan \u00fea earmlican witu and \u00f0a fulan stowa on \u00fe\u00e6re grimman susle on\n\u00d0\u00e6r synd sorhlice tosomne gemencged se \u00ferosmiga lig and se \u00ferece gycela, swi\u00f0e hat and ceald helle\nHwylon \u00fe\u00e6r eagan ungemetum wepa\u00f0 for \u00fe\u00e6s ofnes bryne, hwylon eac \u00fea te\u00f0 for mycclum cyle\n\u00d0uss atelic gewrixl \u00fea earmsceapenan men on worulda woruld wenda\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6rinne on forsworcennesse\nNe by\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6r nan stefn gehyred, buton stearc and heard wop and wanung for wohd\u00e6dum.\nNe by\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6r ansyn gesewen \u00e6nigre wihte, buton \u00fe\u00e6ra deofla, \u00fee cwylma\u00f0 \u00fea earman.\nNe by\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6r aht inne, buton lig and cyle and la\u00f0lic fulnes, ne hi mid heora nosum ne magon naht elles\n\u00d0\u00e6r beo\u00f0 \u00fea waniendan weleras afylde ligspiwelum bryne on \u00feam hellican fyre, and hi w\u00e6lgrimme\nNe bi\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6r leohtes an lytel spearca, \u00feam earmum \u00e6nig frofer; ne arf\u00e6stnys ne sibb ne hopa ne \u00e6nig\nFlyh\u00f0 se frofur aweg, ne by\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6r fultum nan, \u00fe\u00e6t wi\u00f0 \u00fea biteran \u00feing gebeorh m\u00e6ge gefremman.\nNe by\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6r ansyn gemett \u00e6nigre blisse, ac \u00fe\u00e6r bi\u00f0 angryslic ege and fyrhto, sarig mod and swi\u00f0lic\n\u00d0onne beo\u00f0 ealle agene \u00feing \u00feissere worlde, \u00fe\u00e6t leof w\u00e6s \u00e6r, hit by\u00f0 la\u00f0 \u00feonne, and \u00fe\u00e6t werige mod\nAc se by\u00f0 ges\u00e6lig and ofers\u00e6lig, se \u00f0e mid gesyntum swylce cwyldas and witu m\u00e6g wel forbugan and\n\u00de\u00e6r niht ne genim\u00f0 n\u00e6fre \u00feurh \u00feystru \u00fe\u00e6s heofonlican leohtes sciman, ne cym\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6r sorh ne sar ne\nNis \u00f0\u00e6r hryre ne caru ne hreoge tintregu.\nNe by\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6r liget ne la\u00f0lic storm ne winter ne cyle ne \u00feunor.\nNe by\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6r w\u00e6dl ne lyre ne dea\u00f0es gryre ne yrm\u00f0 ne angsumnys ne \u00e6nig gnornung.\nAc \u00fe\u00e6r is ece wuldor and wyr\u00f0mynt and ece lif betweox heahf\u00e6derum and haligum witegum.\nNu, leofan men, hwa is \u00e6fre, \u00fe\u00e6t h\u00e6bbe swa hearde heortan, \u00fe\u00e6t he ne m\u00e6ge him ondr\u00e6don \u00fea\nHw\u00e6t is us la selre, \u00feonne we ealne weg ure synna beton and hi mid \u00e6lmessan georne alyson, for\u00f0am\nSum halig man w\u00e6s gel\u00e6d on gesyh\u00f0e; \u00fea geseah he sume earme sawle ut fundigende of hyre\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 an \u00fe\u00e6ra deofla to hyre: hw\u00e6t is \u00fein \u00feriding?\nHwi nelt \u00f0u ut gan?\nWen ys, \u00fe\u00e6t Michael se heahencgel cume mid engla \u00fereatum and wyle \u00fee geniman of us.\n\u00d0a andwyrde sum o\u00f0er deofol and cw\u00e6\u00f0: nese, ic wat ealle hyre weorc, and ic w\u00e6s d\u00e6ges and nihtes\nSeo earme sawul beseah uppan \u00feone deofol and earmlice clypode: wa me earmre, \u00fe\u00e6t ic \u00e6fre geboren\nEala \u00feu earma lichama and wurma mete, a \u00feu wunne \u00e6fter eor\u00f0licum welum, and a \u00f0u geglengdest \u00fee\n\u00deonne \u00f0u w\u00e6re gl\u00e6d and reod and godes hiwes, \u00feonne w\u00e6s ic blac and swy\u00f0e unrot; \u00feonne \u00feu\nEala \u00feu earma lichama, nu \u00feu scealt gewur\u00f0an to fulan hr\u00e6we and wyrmum to mete; and ic mid sare\nSe lichama ongan \u00fea sw\u00e6tan and mislic hiw bredan.\nAnd se deofol hludre stefne clypode and cw\u00e6\u00f0: stinga\u00f0 stranglic sar on his eagan, for\u00f0am, swa hw\u00e6t\nStinga\u00f0 hine scearplice on \u00feone mu\u00f0, for\u00f0i, swa hw\u00e6t swa hine lyste etan o\u00f0\u00f0e drincan o\u00f0\u00f0e on unnyt\nStinga\u00f0 hine mid sorhlicum sare on his heortan, for\u00f0am \u00fee on hyre ne wunode arf\u00e6stnys ne\n\u00d0a deoflu feredon \u00fea earman sawle \u00fea to \u00feystrum; \u00fea geseah heo be \u00feam wege mycele beorhtnyssa;\nHi cw\u00e6don: ne ongytst \u00f0u, \u00fe\u00e6t hit ys heofonan rices gefea, \u00feanon \u00feu w\u00e6re \u00e6r cumen to \u00feinum\nNu \u00f0u f\u00e6rst \u00feurh \u00fea beorhtan wegas, ac \u00f0u n\u00e6fst \u00fe\u00e6r nane wununge.\nNu \u00f0u gehyrst engla \u00fereatas, and \u00f0u gesihst ealra haligra beorhtnessa, and \u00f0u n\u00e6fst \u00fe\u00e6r nane\nHeo ongan \u00fea wependre stefne cwe\u00fean: wa me earmre, \u00fe\u00e6t ic \u00e6fre middaneardes leoht geseon\n\u00d0a deoflu hi \u00f0a l\u00e6ddon and bescuton hi anum fyrenan dracan innan \u00feone mu\u00f0, and he hi \u00fe\u00e6rrihte\nUton nu, leofan men, gebeorgan us wi\u00f0 swilce eardungstowe and wendon anr\u00e6dlice to urum drihtne\nAnd uton onettan and efstan, \u00fe\u00e6t we mid eallum haligum m\u00e6gnum magon and motan \u00fea deoflican\nWe sceolon gewilnian symle \u00fe\u00e6s ecan lifes, for\u00f0am \u00fee on \u00feam life syndon gode dagas, ne swa\u00feeah\n\u00d0eah \u00fee hwa wylle her on life habban gode dagas, he ne m\u00e6g hi her findan, \u00feeah \u00f0e he si welig for\nUton wendan us to urum drihtne, he us wyle mildelice underfon, gyf we wylla\u00f0 on his naman ure\nAnd uton biddan urne drihten for his myclan mildheortnesse and for ealra his halgena lufon and\nHeofonan heahcyning and ealles middaneardes alysend, gemiltsa us synfullum, swa swa \u00f0in milda\n\u00d0\u00e6r is ece leoht buton \u00feystrum; nis \u00f0\u00e6r adles granung, ac \u00fe\u00e6r is geogo\u00f0 butan ylde; \u00fe\u00e6r is ece lif\nNe bi\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6r unrotnes \u00e6fter gefean, ac \u00fe\u00e6r \u00f0urhwuna\u00f0 aa seo ece bliss; ne by\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6r hungor ne \u00feurst ne\nUton we nu hine mid eallum m\u00e6gne and mid eallum mode lufian, \u00feonne geara\u00f0 he us \u00e6t \u00feam dome.\nSi him wuldor and lof a butan ende on ecnysse, amen.",
